# Infrastructure

## Local dev

- `docker compose up --build` starts the full stack
- Service healthchecks defined in `docker-compose.yml` — preserve them when adding services
- Postgres: TimescaleDB on host port **5433** (not 5432)
- Dev secrets in compose are placeholders — never copy to production

## Service dependencies

```
postgres, redis → governance, detection → proxy → dashboard
ollama → detection (fallback inference)
dns-sinkhole → proxy + detection (shadow AI)
```

## Dockerfiles

- Python services: root context `.`, dockerfile in `proxy/Dockerfile` / `detection/Dockerfile`
- Governance: context `./governance`, own Dockerfile
- Dashboard: build args `VITE_API_URL`, `VITE_GOVERNANCE_URL`

## Helm (production path)

- Chart: `infra/helm/ai-gateway/`
- Values: `values.yaml` — override per environment, not hardcode in templates
- Templates: `proxy.yaml`, `common.yaml` — use `_helpers.tpl` for labels

## Scripts

- `scripts/demo.sh`, `scripts/live_demo_events.sh` — demo orchestration
- `scripts/init-db.sql` — DB bootstrap on first postgres start
- `scripts/run_feature_tests.sh` — integration test runner
